# Provenance and intentional deviations

Every fixture file and screen contract cites the frozen prototype file and the
prototype state names it derives from. This file lists where the
implementation deliberately differs from the prototype and why. Anything not
listed here is expected to match the prototype's behaviour and spacing.

Frozen reference: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL,
page "Refined Native v2", version 134 (version id 1793059808-4929, published
2026-10-26). Files and hashes: [prototype/MANIFEST.sha256](prototype/MANIFEST.sha256).

| # | Prototype | Implementation | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| P1 | Wizard tenant step draws the scan key and Gateway workspace key as text fields (`R2Onboard` `f.cred`) | "Add scan key…" button opens the host's native secret sheet; the step then shows a masked indicator and the vault record id | The web layer never holds a secret (D014, C09 reveal ownership). Visual delta: button plus masked state instead of a field |
| P2 | Rotation panel renders the secret in a readonly input with Reveal/Copy (`R2App` `secretShown`) | Reveal shows the secret in the host secret sheet; Copy goes through the host clipboard; both consume a one-time disclosure token | Invariant I6; same reason as P1 |
| P3 | State lives in one component with `byTenant` (`R2App` `TS/ts/tPatch`) | Core-owned scopes per [state-ownership.md](state-ownership.md) | D014 authority; prototype state model is normative for invariants only |
| P4 | ⌘1–⌘9 are advertised but not bound (canvas rule: no global key handlers) | Native menu defines the shortcuts and dispatches `navigate` | Host owns menus; works under VoiceOver and shows in the menu bar |
| P5 | Sidebar lists Home, Inbox, Harness, Academy, Test Cases, API Client, Administration | Same, backed by Rust feature ids `home`, `inbox`, `harness`, `academy`, `library`, `apiClient`, `administration`; `gateway` and `redTeam` move inside Administration; `sessions`, `import`, `settings` reachable from the palette and Administration | One Rust inventory feeds menu, sidebar and palette |
| P6 | Wizard boards are 1440×900 with a fixed 320px rail | Minimum window 1180×720; rail collapses to icons below 1280 wide | 13-inch displays |
| P7 | Toasts expire on timers always | Persist until dismissed under Reduce Motion | Native acceptance Reduce Motion check |
| P8 | Inbox items, Harness lifecycles, API responses, cases and Academy progress are invented in-component data | Wire fixtures in `packages/desktop-contracts/fixtures/wire`, content derived from the prototype data | Fixtures are the contract test surface; prototype data is never shipped |
| P9 | `TOPICS.injo` added in round 16 as a separate key from detector `inj` | Core topic inventory keys are a distinct type from detector ids | Carries the round-16 fix into the type system |
| P10 | Administration creation label is a per-product single value | Per-tab creation capability and label in `AdminInventory` | Round 16 finding: wrong label on API keys, Security profiles and Logs tabs |
| P11 | Home snooze button hard-codes "Snooze 24 hours" | Item-specific `snoozeLabel` shared by Home and Inbox | Round 16 finding; invariant I11 |
| P12 | API Client Send has no live completion status | Compact `role="status"` region with request name, response code and duration; JSON body outside the live region | Round 16 finding |
| P13 | Tenant switch with an open applied key review leaves disclosure open | Any review exit, including switch, finalises disclosure | Round 16 finding; invariant I6 |
| P14 | Applied injection-override examples show "Not demonstrated" in the Playground | Topic examples classify under the topic key with a profile-aware verdict | Round 16 finding |
| P15 | Import from v1 is a separate destination | Also offered on the wizard tenant step as a secondary action; credentials re-entered via the secret sheet | First run is where an upgrading user needs it |

P10–P14 are the five round-16 Codex items carried as known gaps (see
[DESIGN-V2.md](DESIGN-V2.md) "Known gaps").
# Tokens

The desktop app owns its appearance. A local token file
(`apps/desktop/src/styles/tokens.css`, created in C28) defines these names as
CSS custom properties under `--v2-*`, with the light values on `:root` and the
dark values under `[data-theme="dark"]`. Academy's `--academy-*` variables are
left intact for the embedded learner view; where a shared Academy component
renders inside the new shell, the Academy variable it reads is aliased to the
`--v2-*` value in the shell's scope only. No colour is written inline in a
component.

## Colour (from `L` and `D` in `prototype/R2App.dc.html` line 677–678)

| Token | Light | Dark | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| bg | #f6f2e9 | #1d2021 | Page background (body gets this explicitly) |
| side | #ebe5d8 | #161919 | Sidebar and wizard rail |
| paper | #fbf8f1 | #282828 | Cards, dialogs, sheets |
| inset | #efe9dd | #32302f | Selected row, inset panels, explain track |
| rule | #e0d9ca | #3c3836 | Borders between regions, secondary buttons |
| ctl | #857d6e | #8a7f70 | Control borders (inputs, selects, toggles) — AA against bg and paper |
| ink | #14141a | #ebdbb2 | Primary text |
| soft | #4a463c | #d5c4a1 | Secondary text |
| faint | #635d50 | #bdae93 | Tertiary text, meta lines — still AA at 12px on bg |
| acc | #a33d15 | #fe8019 | Accent: primary buttons, focus ring, selected sidebar item |
| accInk | #ffffff | #1d2021 | Text on accent |
| accSoft | #f4dfd3 | #4a2f1a | Accent tint backgrounds |
| block | #b42318 | #ff6b57 | Verdict Blocked, Critical severity |
| blockBg | #fbe4e1 | #3d1f1c | Blocked background |
| flag | #8a5300 | #fabd2f | Verdict Flagged, Warning severity |
| flagBg | #faeed5 | #3a3019 | Flagged background |
| ok | #1f6f3a | #b8bb26 | Verdict Allowed, success |
| okBg | #def0e3 | #2b2f17 | Success background |
| sel / selInk | = acc / accInk | = acc / accInk | Selected tenant in the switcher |
| get | #245e8f | #83a598 | HTTP method and link colour in the API Client |

Verdicts and severities are never colour alone: every use pairs the colour with
an icon and a word (invariant I9).

## Spacing, type and size

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| page-margin-top | 32px | Every destination's top margin |
| page-margin-x | 44px | Every destination's side margin (wizard main: 34/44/24 add-mode, 32/44/28 first-run) |
| title | 26px / 700 | Destination and wizard step titles |
| card-pad | 18–20px | Card and dialog inner padding |
| gap | 10–12px | Between controls and cards; inner card gap 12px |
| text | 14px | Body |
| text-2 | 12px | Secondary text. 11px only for pills, eyebrows and mono badges |
| control-h | 32px | Inputs, selects, buttons |
| radius | 7px controls, 12px cards | |
| rail-w | 244px | Sidebar and add-tenant wizard rail (first-run wizard rail 320px) |
| reading-max | 860px | Reading width cap for prose and forms |
| focus | 2px solid acc, offset 2px; `data-inset-focus` buttons use offset −4px | Visible focus everywhere |
| window-min | 1180×720 | Rail collapses to icons below 1280 wide; no horizontal scroll anywhere |

## Theme switching

Theme remains Rust-owned (`setAppearance`). The shell sets `data-theme` on the
document root from the observed appearance and `prefers-color-scheme` for
"system". Tokens are the only place a theme value lives.
# UI v2 "Refined Native" — design extraction

This folder is the source of truth for the second-generation desktop
presentation: the shell, first-run wizard, Inbox and reads, reviews,
Administration, Harness, API Client, Test Cases and the Academy embed, as
reviewed on the Claude Design canvas and frozen at version 134 (2026-10-26).

Record: decision D058 in [decisions.md](../../planning/decisions.md). Phase:
P09, chunks C27–C34 ([chunk index](../../planning/chunks/README.md)).

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| [DESIGN-V2.md](DESIGN-V2.md) | Scope, frozen reference, layout rhythm, destinations, error presentation, accessibility additions, budgets, known gaps |
| [tokens.md](tokens.md) | The token table for both themes and the mapping onto Academy variables |
| [state-ownership.md](state-ownership.md) | Every prototype state field assigned to Rust-owned/observed or UI-transient |
| [invariants.md](invariants.md) | The twelve normative rules with their acceptance test ids |
| [screens/](screens/) | One interaction contract per screen family |
| [provenance.md](provenance.md) | Intentional deviations from the prototype, with reasons |
| [prototype/](prototype/) | Frozen copies of the six reviewed R2 files and their SHA-256 manifest. Immutable inputs; never edited |

The canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL, page "Refined
Native v2") is the design record only. After version 134 it is not changed;
further exploration happens on a new page. The prototype's data is invented
and is never shipped; it is used only to write fixture content.
# Shell, Home, tenant switcher, palette, toasts

Source: `prototype/R2App.dc.html` (sidebar markup, `nav`, `switchPatch`,
`requestSwitch`, `palette*`, `toast*`, `top`, Home section). Chunk: C28 (shell,
Home skeleton), C30 (Home attention list backed by Inbox scope).

## Sidebar

- Top: tenant switcher button showing tenant name and environment pill;
  ⌘T opens the list. Entries: every tenant (name, environment, TSG), then
  "Add a tenant…". Selected tenant uses `sel/selInk`.
- Destinations in the order of DESIGN-V2 §5 with icon, label, shortcut hint.
  Unavailable destinations render disabled with their availability reason as
  a tooltip and accessible description, never hidden.
- Bottom: appearance toggle (light/dark/system) and "Show the calls" toggle,
  both dispatching their Rust preference.
- Collapses to icons below 1280px window width.

## Home

- Title "Home" with the tenant name and environment beneath; last-read line
  from `ReadStatus` ("Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete" or
  "· 3 sources partial", warn-styled when partial; "First read pending" on a
  fresh tenant).
- "Needs attention": up to five Inbox items of kind Needs action, each with
  severity (colour + icon + word), title, product, action button that
  navigates with context, Acknowledge, and Snooze whose tooltip and
  accessible name are the item's `snoozeLabel`.
- Product cards for licensed products with their read state; unlicensed
  products are listed once as "Not licensed in this tenant" rather than hidden.
- Playground card (Runtime Security scan): prompt, direction, profile select,
  verdict panel (word + icon + reason + plain explanation). Verdicts are
  profile-aware: a detector not enabled, or a topic not assigned, reads "Not
  detected" with the reason; monitor-only turns Blocked into Flagged with the
  profile named.

## Tenant switch (I1, I2)

- `switchTenant{tenant_id, resolution?}`; the core refuses with
  `SwitchBlocked{pending: {conversation, decision}}` when a Harness decision is
  pending. The UI renders the guard dialog (Archive and switch / Discard and
  switch / Stay) from that payload and re-dispatches with `resolution`.
- Every entry point (switcher, palette, menu, wizard completion) uses the same
  intent. After a switch the new tenant's Home renders from cached scopes within
  100 ms with read status pending until the read lands.

## Command palette

- ⌘K. Entries: destinations from the Rust inventory, tenants, and three actions
  (Navigate, Switch tenant, Read now). Typing filters; Enter dispatches; Escape
  closes and restores focus. Native menu navigation while the palette is open
  closes it first.

## Toasts (I10)

- Kinds ok, info, warn with icon and colour; one visible at a time, newest
  replaces; 6 s expiry (persist under Reduce Motion); optional Undo action
  (snooze). A toast never carries information absent from an observed scope.

## Modals (I8)

- Stack order kept in the shell store; only the topmost is interactive;
  siblings get `aria-hidden`; Escape closes the topmost; focus returns to the
  opener. Detail sheets (transcripts, facts) are modals in this stack.

## Fixtures and tests

- Fixture boards: R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark, R2App default.
- V2-T01, T02, T09, T10, T11; V2-N01, N03, N04, N05.
# First-run wizard and add-tenant sheet

Source: `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html` (steps, `ERR`, `touch`, `vsig`,
`verify`, `opened`, `railCtx`, `mode="add"`), `R2App` `addtenant` overlay.
Chunk: C29. Realises D013 (scan-key-first onboarding).

## Steps (first run)

1. **Welcome** — explains that the app is built entirely on Palo Alto
   Networks' public APIs and exists to show application builders what those
   interfaces make possible; three cards: Built on the public APIs / See the
   calls as you go / Learn by doing. Continue.
2. **Tenant** — name, environment (select), region (select), TSG id,
   Gateway workspace (optional), "Add scan key…" (host secret sheet; required),
   "Add Gateway workspace key…" (optional). Secondary action "Import from
   Prisma AIRS Desktop v1" fills name/environment/TSG from the import intent;
   keys are always re-entered. Validation per field on blur with
   `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`; the Continue button names what is
   missing. After this step the rail shows "Name · Environment · TSG …" under
   its title.
3. **Products** — cards for the six products with licence state read from the
   tenant; select those to read. Red Team is marked read-only.
4. **Verify** — dispatch `verifyTenantSetup`; per-product rows fill as
   `VerifyStep` results stream (pass / warning / fail with reason). The AES
   warning demo and a failed row are fixtures. Fail offers "Fix and verify
   again" (returns to Tenant) or "Continue with warnings"; warnings become
   Inbox items on completion.
5. **Starter packs** (optional) — test-case packs per selected product with
   counts.
6. **Academy account** (optional) — sign in or skip; the trust copy states
   exactly what syncs (Academy progress only).
7. **Done** — summary; "Open Prisma AIRS" is finite (`opening` → done) and
   dispatches `completeOnboarding`.

## Add-tenant sheet (`mode="add"`)

- 1160×780 sheet over the shell, rail 244px, no Welcome or Academy steps,
  Cancel at every step; completion dispatches `addTenant` then `switchTenant`.
  Cancel discards everything except a credential already written by the
  secret sheet, which is shown in Administration as unattached and can be
  removed there.

## Core contract

- `verifyTenantSetup{draft}` → stream of `VerifyStep{product, state, reason}`
  then `VerifyDone{warnings}`.
- `completeOnboarding{name, env, region, ws, tsg, credential_ids, products,
  packs, academy_opt_in, warnings}` writes the tenant profile, product
  selection, packs and Inbox warning items; sets `onboarding=done`.
- `addTenant{...same minus academy}`.
- The core never receives a secret through these intents; `credential_ids`
  reference vault records created by the host secret sheet.

## Fixtures and tests

- Boards: R2On* (one per step, filled and verify variants), R2AddTenant.
- Tests: step validation and invalidation signature; streaming verify order;
  cancel semantics; `onboarding` transitions; V2-N02.
- Live (C29 only): verify against Vulture, reads only, under the designated
  scope.

