# Provenance and intentional deviations

Every fixture file and screen contract cites the frozen prototype file and the
prototype state names it derives from. This file lists where the
implementation deliberately differs from the prototype and why. Anything not
listed here is expected to match the prototype's behaviour and spacing.

Frozen reference: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL,
page "Refined Native v2", version 134 (version id 1793059808-4929, published
2026-10-26). Files and hashes: [prototype/MANIFEST.sha256](prototype/MANIFEST.sha256).

| # | Prototype | Implementation | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| P1 | Wizard tenant step draws the scan key and Gateway workspace key as text fields (`R2Onboard` `f.cred`) | "Add scan key…" button opens the host's native secret sheet; the step then shows a masked indicator and the vault record id | The web layer never holds a secret (D014, C09 reveal ownership). Visual delta: button plus masked state instead of a field |
| P2 | Rotation panel renders the secret in a readonly input with Reveal/Copy (`R2App` `secretShown`) | Reveal shows the secret in the host secret sheet; Copy goes through the host clipboard; both consume a one-time disclosure token | Invariant I6; same reason as P1 |
| P3 | State lives in one component with `byTenant` (`R2App` `TS/ts/tPatch`) | Core-owned scopes per [state-ownership.md](state-ownership.md) | D014 authority; prototype state model is normative for invariants only |
| P4 | ⌘1–⌘9 are advertised but not bound (canvas rule: no global key handlers) | Native menu defines the shortcuts and dispatches `navigate` | Host owns menus; works under VoiceOver and shows in the menu bar |
| P5 | Sidebar lists Home, Inbox, Harness, Academy, Test Cases, API Client, Administration | Same, backed by Rust feature ids `home`, `inbox`, `harness`, `academy`, `library`, `apiClient`, `administration`; `gateway` and `redTeam` move inside Administration; `sessions`, `import`, `settings` reachable from the palette and Administration | One Rust inventory feeds menu, sidebar and palette |
| P6 | Wizard boards are 1440×900 with a fixed 320px rail | Minimum window 1180×720; rail collapses to icons below 1280 wide | 13-inch displays |
| P7 | Toasts expire on timers always | Persist until dismissed under Reduce Motion | Native acceptance Reduce Motion check |
| P8 | Inbox items, Harness lifecycles, API responses, cases and Academy progress are invented in-component data | Wire fixtures in `packages/desktop-contracts/fixtures/wire`, content derived from the prototype data | Fixtures are the contract test surface; prototype data is never shipped |
| P9 | `TOPICS.injo` added in round 16 as a separate key from detector `inj` | Core topic inventory keys are a distinct type from detector ids | Carries the round-16 fix into the type system |
| P10 | Administration creation label is a per-product single value | Per-tab creation capability and label in `AdminInventory` | Round 16 finding: wrong label on API keys, Security profiles and Logs tabs |
| P11 | Home snooze button hard-codes "Snooze 24 hours" | Item-specific `snoozeLabel` shared by Home and Inbox | Round 16 finding; invariant I11 |
| P12 | API Client Send has no live completion status | Compact `role="status"` region with request name, response code and duration; JSON body outside the live region | Round 16 finding |
| P13 | Tenant switch with an open applied key review leaves disclosure open | Any review exit, including switch, finalises disclosure | Round 16 finding; invariant I6 |
| P14 | Applied injection-override examples show "Not demonstrated" in the Playground | Topic examples classify under the topic key with a profile-aware verdict | Round 16 finding |
| P15 | Import from v1 is a separate destination | Also offered on the wizard tenant step as a secondary action; credentials re-entered via the secret sheet | First run is where an upgrading user needs it |

P10–P14 are the five round-16 Codex items carried as known gaps (see
[DESIGN-V2.md](DESIGN-V2.md) "Known gaps").
# Inbox and reads

Source: `R2App` (`ITEMS`, `visibleItems`, `ack`, `snoozed`, `snooze`,
`inboxRows`, `sel`, `startRead`, `recheck`, `toGo`). Chunk: C30.

## Inbox

- Tabs All / Needs action / Updates / Snoozed with counts. Rows: severity
  (colour + icon + word), title, product, source line ("API keys · cached",
  "rotated 07:46"), when, acknowledged mark. Selecting opens the detail pane:
  body, facts table, "Why this matters" explanation, action button (navigates
  with context), Acknowledge / Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze.
- Empty states distinguish "first read pending" from "nothing needs action"
  and name partial sources ("3 of 6 sources were read at 07:45").
- Snooze: per item, core-computed return time. Generic items return in 24 h;
  deadline-bound items (rotation reminder) return one hour before their
  deadline. The label, toast and Snoozed-tab "Returns …" text all state the
  same time (I11).
- Contextual navigation: an item's action carries a target (screen, product,
  tab, conversation). Into an ended conversation it sets a transient hint
  offering "Open the saved transcript" and "Start a new investigation".

## Reads (I4)

- `readTenant` runs a finite read of every selected product; `ReadStatus`
  carries per-product state (pending, ok, partial, needsRole), last-read
  time and counts. First read on a fresh tenant shows pending everywhere.
- Completion toast: ok "Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete" or
  warn "· 3 sources partial"; for fresh tenants "· 1 product still needs a
  role" or "· no activity yet in <tenant>". `recheckProduct` after a role is
  granted shows an info toast and re-reads.

## Core contract

- Scope `InboxItem{id, kind, severity, title, product, source, when, body,
  facts, action_target, explanation, deadline?, snooze_return?, acknowledged}`
  per tenant; intents `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`,
  `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`.
- The rotation reminder is a distinct item id from the expiry alert (I7).

## Fixtures and tests

- Board R2Inbox. Tests V2-R02, R04, R08, R09; V2-T04, T12, T13; V2-N02.
# Reviews, Administration and key rotation

Source: `R2App` (`REVIEWS`, `rvKind`, `canApply`, `doApply`, `appliedKey`,
`appliedOther`, `TOPICS`, `PROFILES`, `verdictFor`, `T` admin tables, API keys
row actions). Chunk: C31.

## Administration

- Accordion of six products: AI Runtime Security, AI Red Teaming (read-only),
  AI Supply Chain, AI Gateway, Agentic Identity Security, Agentic Endpoint
  Security. Each expands to tabs from `AdminInventory` with per-tab creation
  capability and label ("New topic…", "New API key…", "New provider…"; none on
  Logs and Results). Unlicensed products show their state, not nothing.
- Tables: columns per tab, row actions "Edit…", "Rotate…", "Finish
  rotation…", "View", "Results". Read-only products never offer a change.
- Security profiles and Custom topics derive "Used by" from one topic
  inventory; detector ids and topic keys are distinct types.

## Review (I3)

- Opened by `openReview{kind, resource}`; the scope carries tenant, resource,
  before/after diff lines, impact ("Used by 3 security profiles: …; takes
  effect on their next scan"), and the typed-name requirement.
- The UI shows the diff, impact, a text field "Type <name> to confirm" and
  Apply (disabled until match). `confirmReview{review_id, typed}` is
  validated in the core: wrong name, different tenant or changed context
  refuses with the reason, and the UI shows a warn toast naming the tenant.
- Applied panel (non-key): "Live. The item was read back." with name,
  revision, time, tenant. Done.
- Any review exit (Done, Escape, tenant switch) clears `secretVisible` and
  finalises disclosure (I6).

## Key rotation (I6, I7)

Three panel states after `confirmReview` on a key:

1. **Key issued · rotation not finished** — secret controls (Reveal via host
   secret sheet, Copy via host clipboard, both consuming the disclosure
   token), "Shown once here…" note, grace line "Old key valid until
   <deadline with timezone>", actions Finish later / Application updated ·
   finish rotation.
2. **Rotation in progress · key issued earlier** — no secret controls; text
   says the secret is available only from the Keychain on this Mac; "Where is
   the secret?" explains the Keychain location; grace line and the same two
   actions.
3. **Rotation complete** — revocation time (stored once at confirmation and
   never recomputed), "the Inbox reminder cleared"; Done only.

Side effects: issuing creates Inbox item `rotation-<key>` (Needs action,
deadline-bound snooze) and clears any acknowledgment or snooze on the expiry
alert; the key row reads "Review · key issued, deploy before <deadline>" with
action "Finish rotation…"; confirming completes the row ("Active · rotation
complete <time>"), clears the item and fires the completion toast.

## Playground verdicts

- Detector results and topic matches are independent. A profile without the
  detector, or without the topic assigned, yields "Not detected" with the
  reason; monitor-only turns Blocked into Flagged; applying a topic never
  suppresses an enabled detector. The applied topic's example prompts classify
  under the topic and show Flagged when assigned.

## Fixtures and tests

- Boards R2Admin, R2Review. Tests V2-R03, R06, R07; V2-T03, T06, T07, T08.
- Live (C31 only): one topic review apply and read-back against Redtail under
  the `airs-v2-c25-` prefix, with cleanup.
# Harness

Source: `R2App` (`CONVOS` blocks/mcp/keys, `decs`, `ended`, `archiveActive`,
`sendDraft`, `startNewConvo`, `convoHint`, `follows`), boards R2Harness,
R2Harness2, R2Harness3. Chunk: C32.

The screen is a re-skin of the existing Harness engine, sessions, decisions,
MCP and sign-in modules; the conversation and decision model is unchanged.

## Layout

- Title row "Harness" with tenant and engine status; left rail of conversations
  (lifecycle seeds appear only on non-fresh fixture tenants; user conversations
  titled from their first message; archived ones marked ended); main
  transcript; composer with a draft per conversation.
- Prerequisites checklist (tenant, management client, Gateway workspace,
  company sign-in) stays visible until satisfied (D057 F05).

## Lifecycles (fixtures)

1. **blocks** — "Why were 14 prompts blocked on claims-triage overnight?":
   tool call `list_security_events` (read-only, in-page Approve/Decline),
   result summary, recommendation, follow-up "Open the review" that opens the
   injection-override topic review.
2. **mcp** — a workspace MCP tool call that writes (native confirmation
   sheet), result, follow-up to Administration.
3. **keys** — rotation investigation ending in "Rotate…" follow-up; the
   follow-up text reflects the rotation state (issued vs complete).

Each has approve, decline, end and follow-up paths. Declining records the
decision and the assistant's declined text; ending seals the session
(`endConversation` → archive id) and the rail shows it ended.

## Rules

- A fresh tenant's first send creates a user conversation (I12); sending in an
  ended conversation creates a new one.
- Contextual navigation into an ended conversation shows a hint with "Open the
  saved transcript" (archived transcript detail) and "Start a new
  investigation" (new conversation prefilled with the opening question). The
  hint clears on any navigation.
- A pending decision blocks tenant switch (I1).

## Fixtures and tests

- Boards R2Harness (blocks), R2Harness2 (mcp), R2Harness3 (keys). Tests
  V2-R01, V2-T01, T13, plus approve/decline/end/follow-up per lifecycle.
# API Client and Test Cases

Source: `R2App` (`REQ`, `hist`, `send`, `rawJson`, `CASES`, `packCases`,
`caseRows`, `runScan`). Chunk: C33. Both are re-skins of the existing
workbench and library modules to the layout rhythm.

## API Client

- Title row, request tabs (named requests per product), method/URL line with
  `get` colour, Send (32px), response pane with status, duration and body;
  history list of immutable snapshots (I5).
- After Send, a compact `role="status"` region announces "<request> · <code>
  · <duration>"; the JSON body is outside the live region.
- "Show the calls" panel reuses this response renderer elsewhere.

## Test Cases

- Title row, filter by product, search, paged table (name, product, input,
  last result as verdict colour + icon + word), Run; pack-sourced cases carry
  their pack name. Running a case sets the Playground's prompt and profile and
  scans; results are stored per case.

## Fixtures and tests

- Boards R2Api, R2Cases. Tests V2-R05, V2-T05, plus status-region and paging.
