     1	# UI v2 "Refined Native" — design specification
     2	
     3	Status: C27 deliverable, reviewed at the 9/10 bar (D058). This document and
     4	its companions ([tokens](tokens.md), [state ownership](state-ownership.md),
     5	[invariants](invariants.md), [screens](screens/), [provenance](provenance.md))
     6	are what every P09 chunk is judged against. The existing
     7	[DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md) remains authoritative for the native authority
     8	interface, transport, Academy presentation ownership and the Harness; this
     9	document changes only how the desktop presents those.
    10	
    11	## 1. Scope and deliverable
    12	
    13	The reviewed prototype is extracted in three layers, in order:
    14	
    15	1. **Spec** (C27, this folder): tokens, screen inventory, state ownership,
    16	   invariants, interaction contracts, copy, provenance, acceptance criteria.
    17	2. **TypeScript presentation** (C28–C29, then per-destination chunks): the new
    18	   shell and screens in `apps/desktop`, built against wire fixtures and the
    19	   mock runtime, behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag.
    20	3. **Rust contract** (within each destination chunk): the intents, scopes and
    21	   refusals the screens need, implemented over existing desktop-core services
    22	   and exported through ts-rs.
    23	
    24	The first implementation slice is the shell plus the first-run wizard and
    25	add-tenant sheet (C28–C29). Harness, Inbox/reads, reviews/Administration, API
    26	Client, Test Cases and the Academy embed follow (C30–C34). The legacy shell,
    27	its feature-view switch, the flag and the legacy native acceptance scripts are
    28	removed in C34; the phase is not complete while any destination renders only
    29	in the legacy shell.
    30	
    31	## 2. Frozen reference
    32	
    33	Canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL, page "Refined Native
    34	v2", version 134. The six R2 files are copied verbatim under
    35	[prototype/](prototype/) with SHA-256 hashes in `MANIFEST.sha256`. They are
    36	immutable inputs. Codex scored the prototype 8/10 on rounds 4–16; the five
    37	open round-16 items are carried as known gaps (§9) and closed in
    38	implementation, not by further prototype rounds.
    39	
    40	## 3. Architecture fit
    41	
    42	- **Authority** stays with desktop-core (D014). The UI dispatches intents and
    43	  observes scopes through the existing two-command Tauri bridge. Every
    44	  prototype state field is assigned in [state-ownership.md](state-ownership.md);
    45	  no surviving state is UI-owned, and no state goes to browser storage.
    46	- **Contract**: new intents, scopes and refusals are Rust types with ts-rs
    47	  derives, regenerated by `xtask bindings`. A hand-written parser is added to
    48	  the contracts client only where runtime validation beyond the type is needed.
    49	- **Shell flag**: `ShellSnapshot.ui_variant` (`legacy` | `v2`) and
    50	  `ShellSnapshot.onboarding` (`needed` | `inProgress` | `done`) are Rust-owned,
    51	  fixture-able and seedable by native acceptance. The React root switches on
    52	  them.
    53	- **Navigation inventory**: one Rust list (feature ids with availability,
    54	  label, shortcut index and sidebar membership) feeds the native menu, the
    55	  sidebar and the command palette. Feature ids gain `home` and `inbox`;
    56	  `library` is shown as "Test Cases"; `gateway` and `redTeam` render inside
    57	  Administration's accordion; `sessions`, `import` and `settings` stay
    58	  reachable from the palette and Administration.
    59	- **Shortcuts** ⌘1–⌘9 are defined by the native menu, which dispatches
    60	  `navigate`; the sidebar displays the menu's truth.
    61	- **Transient state**: a small zustand store per screen family (shell, wizard,
    62	  inbox, admin, harness, workbench); React state only for form fields.
    63	- **Tokens**: local `--v2-*` custom properties ([tokens.md](tokens.md));
    64	  Academy variables untouched for the embedded learner view.
    65	- **Copy**: one `copy.ts` per screen family exporting constants; tests assert
    66	  exact strings. The voice is the wizard's: this app is built entirely on
    67	  Palo Alto Networks' public APIs and exists to show application builders what
    68	  those interfaces make possible; it explains the API call as you go.
    69	- **Show the calls**: a Rust-owned preference reveals, for each action, the
    70	  request and response as the diagnostics module already redacts them
    71	  (credential ids in place of secrets, a note that the core attaches the real
    72	  header). Default on until onboarding completes.
    73	
    74	## 4. Layout rhythm
    75	
    76	Shared by every destination, the wizard and the add-tenant sheet:
    77	
    78	- 32px top and 44px side page margins; 26px/700 titles; 18–20px card
    79	  padding; 10–12px gaps; 32px controls; 14px body, 12px secondary (11px only
    80	  pills, eyebrows and mono badges); 860px reading cap; 244px rail (first-run
    81	  wizard rail 320px).
    82	- Minimum window 1180×720. Below 1280 wide the rail collapses to icons with
    83	  tooltips; nothing scrolls horizontally.
    84	- Tool workspaces (Harness, API Client) have a title row like every other
    85	  destination; no destination is exempt from the rhythm.
    86	
    87	## 5. Destinations
    88	
    89	| Sidebar | Feature id | Shortcut | Contract |
    90	|---|---|---|---|
    91	| Home | `home` (new) | ⌘1 | [screens/shell.md](screens/shell.md) |
    92	| Inbox | `inbox` (new) | ⌘2 | [screens/inbox-reads.md](screens/inbox-reads.md) |
    93	| Harness | `harness` | ⌘3 | [screens/harness.md](screens/harness.md) |
    94	| Academy | `academy` | ⌘4 | [screens/academy.md](screens/academy.md) |
    95	| Test Cases | `library` | ⌘5 | [screens/api-client-test-cases.md](screens/api-client-test-cases.md) |
    96	| API Client | `apiClient` | ⌘6 | same |
    97	| Administration | `administration` (+ `gateway`, `redTeam` inside) | ⌘7 | [screens/reviews-administration.md](screens/reviews-administration.md) |
    98	| Tenant switcher | — | ⌘T | [screens/shell.md](screens/shell.md) |
    99	| Command palette | — | ⌘K | same |
   100	| First-run wizard, add-tenant sheet | — | — | [screens/wizard.md](screens/wizard.md) |
   101	
   102	Red Team is read-only everywhere. Gamification appears only inside the Academy
   103	embed.
   104	
   105	## 6. Error presentation
   106	
   107	- **Refusal** (core refused an intent): warn toast with the refusal reason and
   108	  the tenant named; never a modal. Guard-type refusals (tenant switch with a
   109	  pending decision) render their dialog from the refusal payload.
   110	- **Delivery unknown**: inline "not confirmed" state on the control that
   111	  dispatched, with Retry; the control is not reset.
   112	- **Contract violation**: generic warn toast; detail to diagnostics.
   113	
   114	## 7. Accessibility additions
   115	
   116	The native acceptance checklist gains four items that every P09 chunk's
   117	acceptance script asserts: accent-colour focus ring on every focusable
   118	control (inset variant where declared); `role="status"` live regions for read
   119	status, API send completion and review apply; one topmost modal with
   120	`aria-hidden` siblings and focus return; toasts persist under Reduce Motion.
   121	Existing requirements (keyboard-only, VoiceOver attributes, 150%/200% zoom,
   122	contrast AA) continue to apply to every changed screen.
   123	
   124	## 8. Budgets
   125	
   126	Existing `budgets.json` entries carry unchanged. New: a tenant switch renders
   127	the new tenant's Home from cached scopes within 100 ms, with read status
   128	showing pending until the read lands (measured by the C30 workload).
   129	
   130	## 9. Known gaps carried from the prototype
   131	
   132	Codex round 16 (score 8) left five items, closed by the chunk named:
   133	
   134	1. Secret disclosure survives a tenant switch with the key review open → I6, C31.
   135	2. Applied injection-override examples show "Not demonstrated" → topic
   136	   verdicts keyed separately from detectors, profile-aware, C31.
   137	3. Administration creation labels from a per-product single value → per-tab
   138	   `AdminInventory` capability and label, C31.
   139	4. Home snooze tooltip hard-codes "Snooze 24 hours" → shared item
   140	   `snoozeLabel`, I11, C30.
   141	5. API Client Send announces nothing → `role="status"` completion region, C33.
   142	
   143	## 10. Verification
   144	
   145	- Behaviour: Vitest + Testing Library component tests, one named fixture per
   146	  prototype wrapper board (R2Inbox, R2Harness ×3 lifecycles, R2Api, R2Academy,
   147	  R2Cases, R2Admin, R2Review, R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark, R2AddTenant,
   148	  R2On* steps), so every reviewed state has a test.
   149	- Contract: Rust integration tests per invariant (`V2-Rxx`).
   150	- Native: the existing Accessibility-API scripts, extended per chunk, plus a
   151	  screenshot evidence set per chunk at 100% and 200% zoom in both themes filed
   152	  under `evidence/Cxx/screens/`.
   153	- Live: only C29 (wizard verify against Vulture, reads only) and C31 (review
   154	  apply against Redtail under the `airs-v2-c25-` prefix) run live, inside the
   155	  scope the owner designated on 2026-10-25. Every other chunk runs on fixtures
